  "scope": "leselang-observe read-only projections, mutation observation DTOs and debugger cancellation-plan inspection use the existing product adapter request and its full static admission without linking leselang-vm or SQLite. The optional vm-bridge exposes the original public cancellation functions; sqlite-journal preserves the released default and forwards durable storage support. Actual normal/build/dev dependency closures distinguish read-only, memory bridge, default and explicit SQLite. The three original function blocks (mutation, plan inspection, complete log/debugger projection and sanitizer) are byte-identical to the recorded Git baseline. Existing live-VM tests are retained under the bridge; five additional public read-only tests use received data without an evaluator. Two bridge tests preserve dry-run image admission and rejection of unknown or altered live images without attributing an audit, then verify original-state cancellation and idempotent audit timestamps. The 42 actual daemon debugger tests pass. Static decoding/projection/inspection and Applied DTOs do not authenticate grants, prove a live continuation or settle work. Cargo features are additive, not a security boundary. The observer remains product-specific, and complete host-neutral durable VM recovery and full repository extraction remain open. Native source checkpoint verification is rerun unchanged; its manifest still reports incomplete full-VM/extraction gates.",
